    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d188">

                <pb facs="0330" n="245" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg245"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.62/80: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wallace</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-15T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 15,
                                1919, 4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>9343. Department’s 9263.<anchor n="15" xml:id="d188-f1"/></p>
                <p>Since need for American Commissioner in Berlin is of extreme importance Dresel
                    should leave immediately on signature of protocol <pb facs="0331" n="246"
                        xml:id="pg246"/> by Germans and Department should be informed of exact date
                    of departure. If it appears to you wise considering all circumstances for him to
                    leave at an earlier date explain facts to Department in order that proper
                    instructions may be cabled.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
